{
  "name": "Find broken external links in WordPress posts and email a report",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c4fda302-eabb-53c9-8119-259ef533337d",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -200,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 280,
        "content": "## Find broken external links in WordPress posts\n\nReads your latest published posts, collects the external links inside them, checks each link with a lightweight HEAD request, and builds a report of broken links and links that need a manual look. The report can be emailed with Gmail.\n\n**Email is OFF by default.** Set `emailReport` to true in the Config node to send it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "47c1ef33-e9ff-5ed7-ac13-067b890053e1",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        300,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## Setup\n\n1. Create a WordPress Application Password and add a **Basic Auth** credential in n8n (username + Application Password).\n2. Select it in the Get published posts node.\n3. Edit the Config node: `siteUrl` (no trailing slash), `postsToScan`, `maxLinksPerRun`, `requestTimeoutSeconds`.\n4. Optional: add a **Gmail** credential, select it in the Gmail node, set `reportEmail` and `emailReport` = true.\n5. Run manually first and read the output of Build report."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "aed2ae40-bc83-5222-a9a0-0a86d7c5abe2",
      "name": "Reading the results",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        840,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Reading the results\n\n- **broken:** no response, timeout, or a 4xx/5xx status.\n- **review:** 401, 403, 405, 429 or 999. Some sites block automated checks, so open these links yourself.\n- **ok:** the link answered normally.\n\nOnly external links are checked. Links to your own domain are skipped."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f154de56-f829-59ed-84e3-e1b14cb98c7b",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
        -200,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "24d575be-f825-5afa-8463-c9db965c406a",
      "name": "Every Monday 9am",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        -200,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 9
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "46ac967a-3d49-50f8-8bee-15cf57ba5229",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        40,
        540
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "7bff96cc-97a1-553f-acdd-7bfaf8a0d544",
              "name": "siteUrl",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "https://YOUR_SITE_URL"
            },
            {
              "id": "546c0858-ae93-5872-9d70-fa71a33bc58f",
              "name": "postsToScan",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 20
            },
            {
              "id": "1b85a09e-603d-5cac-a9a8-071ca3d59745",
              "name": "maxLinksPerRun",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 40
            },
            {
              "id": "b526aec4-5c81-5635-b552-af48bd8133d6",
              "name": "requestTimeoutSeconds",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 10
            },
            {
              "id": "f6a8457e-b3a3-5190-855c-3df63eaf53be",
              "name": "emailReport",
              "type": "boolean",
              "value": false
            },
            {
              "id": "c85c8f81-d681-58a1-a07d-dff61b13d305",
              "name": "reportEmail",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "user@example.com"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "b636b605-2bc3-5da7-bb4a-205befe6208b",
      "name": "Get published posts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        280,
        540
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $('Config').first().json.siteUrl }}/wp-json/wp/v2/posts",
        "method": "GET",
        "options": {},
        "sendQuery": true,
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpBasicAuth",
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "status",
              "value": "publish"
            },
            {
              "name": "per_page",
              "value": "={{ $('Config').first().json.postsToScan }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "orderby",
              "value": "modified"
            },
            {
              "name": "order",
              "value": "desc"
            },
            {
              "name": "_fields",
              "value": "id,link,title,content"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "7b0a1842-019e-5c2a-a001-decc4f58df4b",
      "name": "Extract external links",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        520,
        540
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const cfg = $('Config').first().json;\nlet siteHost = '';\ntry { siteHost = new URL(cfg.siteUrl).hostname.replace(/^www\\./, ''); } catch (e) {}\nconst seen = new Set();\nconst out = [];\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const post = item.json;\n  const html = post.content && post.content.rendered ? post.content.rendered : '';\n  const re = /href=[\"'](https?:\\/\\/[^\"'#\\s]+)[\"']/gi;\n  let match;\n  while ((match = re.exec(html)) !== null) {\n    const url = match[1].replace(/&amp;/g, '&');\n    let host = '';\n    try { host = new URL(url).hostname.replace(/^www\\./, ''); } catch (e) { continue; }\n    if (host === siteHost) continue;\n    const key = post.id + '|' + url;\n    if (seen.has(key)) continue;\n    seen.add(key);\n    out.push({\n      json: {\n        postId: post.id,\n        postTitle: post.title && post.title.rendered ? post.title.rendered : '',\n        postUrl: post.link,\n        linkUrl: url,\n      },\n    });\n    if (out.length >= Number(cfg.maxLinksPerRun)) return out;\n  }\n}\nreturn out;\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "9ee1e923-6546-5713-88dd-517fb39ccf2d",
      "name": "Check link",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        760,
        540
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $json.linkUrl }}",
        "method": "HEAD",
        "options": {
          "timeout": "={{ Number($('Config').first().json.requestTimeoutSeconds) * 1000 }}",
          "batching": {
            "batch": {
              "batchSize": 5,
              "batchInterval": 500
            }
          },
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true,
              "fullResponse": true
            }
          }
        },
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "User-Agent",
              "value": "Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; n8n-link-checker)"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b11c387d-fdbf-530e-ac7f-e7ef9b23d9bf",
      "name": "Classify results",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1000,
        540
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const links = $('Extract external links').all();\nreturn $input.all().map((item, i) => {\n  const src = links[i].json;\n  const code = Number(item.json.statusCode || 0);\n  let status = 'ok';\n  let detail = code ? String(code) : '';\n  if (item.json.error || !code) {\n    status = 'broken';\n    const err = item.json.error;\n    detail = (err && (err.message || err.description || String(err))) || 'No response';\n  } else if ([401, 403, 405, 429, 999].includes(code)) {\n    status = 'review';\n  } else if (code >= 400) {\n    status = 'broken';\n  }\n  return { json: { ...src, status, detail: String(detail).slice(0, 200) } };\n});\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "e0fe5ea8-f460-5455-ae44-9f3a1932b8f5",
      "name": "Build report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1240,
        540
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const all = $input.all().map((i) => i.json);\nconst rows = all.filter((r) => r.status !== 'ok');\nconst esc = (s) => String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');\nconst broken = rows.filter((r) => r.status === 'broken');\nconst review = rows.filter((r) => r.status === 'review');\nconst toRow = (r) =>\n  '<tr><td>' + esc(r.postTitle) + '</td><td><a href=\"' + esc(r.linkUrl) + '\">' + esc(r.linkUrl) +\n  '</a></td><td>' + esc(r.status) + '</td><td>' + esc(r.detail) + '</td></tr>';\nconst table = rows.length\n  ? '<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Post</th><th>Link</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr>' +\n    rows.map(toRow).join('') + '</table>'\n  : '<p>No broken links found.</p>';\nconst html =\n  '<p>Checked ' + all.length + ' external links. Broken: ' + broken.length + '. Need manual review: ' + review.length + '.</p>' + table;\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      subject: 'WordPress link check: ' + broken.length + ' broken, ' + review.length + ' to review',\n      checked: all.length,\n      brokenCount: broken.length,\n      reviewCount: review.length,\n      hasIssues: rows.length > 0,\n      html,\n    },\n  },\n];\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "be409b65-2190-5899-86b1-a19208d5018c",
      "name": "Send report email?",
